  "notes": "Describes something or someone positioned between two things, acting as an intermediary or intervening force. Often used in formal writing and news to describe hidden factors or middlemen in a situation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {第三者|だいさんしゃ}が{介在|かいざい}する: a third party intervenes\n- {利害|りがい}が{介在|かいざい}する: interests are involved\n- {感情|かんじょう}が{介在|かいざい}する: emotions come into play\n- {仲介者|ちゅうかいしゃ}の{介在|かいざい}: involvement of a mediator\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {仲介|ちゅうかい}: mediation, brokerage — focuses on actively facilitating between parties\n- {介入|かいにゅう}: intervention — implies more forceful or deliberate involvement\n- {媒介|ばいかい}: transmission, mediation — often used for disease vectors or agents that convey something",
